# learning_service — Cursor rules

`learning_service` is a Spring Boot 4 / Java 25 microservice that records
user learning progress for the Education Platform. It owns no course
content and no user identity — it consumes `userId`, `courseId`, and
`lessonId` as opaque UUIDs and exposes its own HTTP API. It is reached by
clients through `api_gateway` at `/api/learning/...` and listens on
`8082` directly.

Build system is Gradle with the Groovy DSL (`build.gradle`, not
`build.gradle.kts`). PostgreSQL is on `localhost:5437` with
`hibernate.ddl-auto: validate` and `spring.jpa.open-in-view: false`.
Liquibase changesets under `deploy/liquibase/changelog/` are the source
of truth for the schema.

Always read `learning_service/AGENTS.md`, `learning_service/CLAUDE.md`,
and `learning_service/README.md` before editing.

## Layout

```
src/main/java/org/example/learning_service/
  domain/
    base/             BaseEntity, BaseValueObject, BaseDomainService,
                      base/exceptions/ValidateException
    enrollment/       Enrollment (root), LessonCompletion, vo/, services/
    certificate/      Certificate (root), services/
    activity/         UserStudyDay (root), services/
  application/
    ports/            EnrollmentRepo, CertificateRepo, StudyActivityRepo,
                      TransactionManager
    interactors/<aggregate>/<operation>/
                      <Operation>Command, <Operation>Interactor,
                      <Operation>View
    interactors/mappers/   domain/view mappers used by interactors
    exceptions/       use-case-level exceptions
    certificate/      CertificateStubS3Url (S3 stub)
  infrastructure/
    adapters/persistence/      *RepoJpaAdapter implements *Repo
    adapters/transactions/     SpringTransactionManagerAdapter
    persistence/repositories/  *SpringDataRepo (Spring Data JPA)
    persistence/mappers/       *PersistenceMapper (domain <-> JPA)
    persistence/models/<aggregate>/  Hibernate* JPA entities
  presentation/http/v1/
    <aggregate>/<operation>/{dto,handlers}
    exception_handlers/   ApiExceptionHandler, ErrorResponse
    mappers/              *MapperQuery (view -> response DTO)
  setup/config_beans/<aggregate>/   *BeansConfig
```

## Three bounded contexts

```
+--------------+--------------------------+----------------------+
| Context      | Aggregate root           | Port                 |
+--------------+--------------------------+----------------------+
| enrollment   | Enrollment (+ Lesson-    | EnrollmentRepo       |
|              | Completion entity)       |                      |
| certificate  | Certificate              | CertificateRepo      |
| activity     | UserStudyDay             | StudyActivityRepo    |
+--------------+--------------------------+----------------------+
```

Each context has its own folder under `domain/`, `application/interactors/`,
`infrastructure/persistence/models/`, `presentation/http/v1/`, and
`setup/config_beans/`. Do not flatten or merge them.

## Hard rules

- Domain is pure Java. Do not import Spring, `jakarta.persistence.*`,
  Jackson, or any web/JPA type in `domain/`. Domain entities extend
  `BaseEntity`, value objects extend `BaseValueObject`, domain services
  extend `BaseDomainService`. Validation throws `ValidateException`.
- State changes go through aggregate methods. Lesson completion goes
  through the `Enrollment` aggregate (`addLessonCompletion(...)` plus
  `updatedAt` bookkeeping inside the `complete_lesson` interactor),
  never through a setter on `LessonCompletion` from outside. Certificate
  issuance goes through the `create_certificate` interactor.
- `CertificateStubS3Url` (`application/certificate/`) is a stub. Do not
  import the AWS SDK or any object-storage client from an interactor. To
  wire real storage, add a `CertificateStorage` port in
  `application/ports/`, implement it under `infrastructure/adapters/`,
  and wire it in `setup/config_beans/certificate/`.
- Activity is updated transactionally inside the enrollment interactors
  (`complete_lesson` increments the matching `UserStudyDay`,
  `leave_course` decrements it). Controllers must not write to
  `StudyActivityRepo` directly; activity changes follow lesson events
  through the enrollment use cases.
- Every interactor wraps its side effects in
  `TransactionManager.inTransaction(...)`. Do not put `@Transactional`
  on an interactor and do not inject a Spring Data repository,
  `EntityManager`, or `JpaRepository` into one — go through the
  `application/ports/*Repo` interface.
- Cross-context references are UUIDs. `Enrollment` holds `userId`,
  `courseId`, and lessons hold `lessonId` as `UUID` values. No shared
  JPA entity with `course_service` or `user_service` is allowed.
- Controllers depend only on an interactor and the matching
  `*MapperQuery`. They never return application `*View` records or
  `Hibernate*` JPA entities — always map to a response DTO under
  `presentation/http/v1/<aggregate>/<operation>/dto/`.
- New use cases register as a `@Bean` in the matching
  `setup/config_beans/<aggregate>/<Aggregate>BeansConfig.java`.
  Interactors are not `@Component`.

## Tests

- Test profile is `application-test.yaml` (H2 in PostgreSQL compatibility
  mode, `ddl-auto: create-drop`).
- Mirror the package layout under `src/test/java/...`.
- Slice the test by layer: domain tests do not need Spring; interactor
  tests use port doubles; persistence tests use `@DataJpaTest` against H2.

## Anti-patterns

- Annotating an interactor with `@Transactional` instead of using
  `TransactionManager`.
- Calling a `*SpringDataRepo` or `EntityManager` from an interactor.
- Placing Spring or JPA annotations in `domain/`.
- Returning `Hibernate*` entities or application `*View` records from a
  `@RestController`.
- Mixing two contexts (e.g. enrollment + certificate) in a single
  `BeansConfig`, single handler, or single folder.
- Importing AWS SDK or any S3 client in place of `CertificateStubS3Url`.

## Validation

Run from `learning_service/`:

```
./gradlew build
./gradlew check
./gradlew test
./gradlew bootRun
```

Swagger UI: `http://localhost:8082/swagger-ui.html`.
OpenAPI JSON: `http://localhost:8082/v3/api-docs`.
